{"id": "EUVD-2026-97441", "enisaUuid": "3c8dedff-f844-3008-8d15-51c2aef53524", "description": "LogicalDOC Community Edition through 9.3 contains an improper authorization vulnerability in the PswRecovery servlet that fails to bind password recovery tickets to the requesting user. Attackers can obtain a ticket for their own account and reuse it with any userId, including administrators, to reset victims' passwords, lock them out, and reveal their email addresses.", "datePublished": "2026-10-12T13:39:45", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-18T12:03:15", "baseScore": 5.3, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:L/UI:N/VC:L/VI:L/VA:L/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://github.com/logicaldoc/community/discussions/119", "https://github.com/logicaldoc/community/commit/afc8554e6654865295bffc8f080c7cb899caf057", "https://github.com/logicaldoc/community/blob/9.3/logicaldoc-webapp/src/main/java/com/logicaldoc/web/PswRecovery.java#L101", "https://github.com/logicaldoc/community", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/logicaldoc-community-edition-through-9.3-forced-password-reset-via-unbound-pswrecovery-ticket"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-109204", "GHSA-75r5-9xr9-27w7"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.2, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "e7a9b063-15a4-32a5-8f0e-9106a79b6c65", "product": {"name": "LogicalDOC Community Edition", "vendor": {"name": "LogicalDOC"}}, "product_version": "0 \u22649.3"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "f405b543-f750-32b7-aa1c-56d6b354fb88", "vendor": {"name": "LogicalDOC"}}], "isExploited": false}